      "rev_n_1_5b2bbf_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_5b2bbf_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_5b2bbf",
        "thought_text": "Check if the sum of all candies is even; if not, output No immediately. If even, check if any single pack equals half the total or if the sum of any two packs equals half the total.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507866.4526968
      },
      "rev_n_2_6d49c9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_6d49c9_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_6d49c9",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the total sum S. The target for each student is S/2. Iterate through all possible subsets of packs (empty, {a}, {b}, {c}, {a,b}, {a,c}, {b,c}, {a,b,c}) and see if any subset sums to S/2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507866.4527113
      },
      "rev_n_3_ba5c1b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_ba5c1b_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_ba5c1b",
        "thought_text": "Since there are only 3 packs, hardcode the specific conditions: either a+b=c, a+c=b, b+c=a, or a=b=c (which implies a+b=c is false but a=b=c means one gets one pack and the other gets two equal packs? No, if a=b=c, total=3a, odd unless a=0 which is not allowed. Wait, if a=b=c, total=3a. Half is 1.5a. Impossible. So only cases where one pack equals sum of other two work. Actually, if a=b, then a+b=2a. If c=2a, then a+b=c works. If a=b=c, impossible. So just check if max(a,b,c) == sum(others).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507866.4527192
      },
      "rev_n_4_c08e17_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_c08e17_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_c08e17",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the total sum of candies. If the sum is odd, it's impossible to split equally, so output No. If even, check if any single pack equals half the sum or if the sum of any two packs equals half the sum. If either condition is met, output Yes; otherwise, No.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "8498350670551273305",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507885.8502982
      },
      "rev_n_5_080daf_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_080daf_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_080daf",
        "thought_text": "Since there are only three packs, iterate through all possible distributions: one student gets 0 packs, 1 pack, 2 packs, or 3 packs. The other student gets the remainder. Check if the sum of candies for both students is equal in any valid distribution where neither gets zero packs (since the problem implies distributing packs between two students, though technically 0 vs 3 is a distribution, the equal sum constraint usually implies non-trivial splits or just checking sum equality regardless). Actually, simpler: just check if any subset sum equals total_sum / 2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "8498350670551273305",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507885.850316
      },
      "rev_n_6_402e75_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_402e75_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_402e75",
        "thought_text": "Sort the three values a, b, c. The only way to split three items into two groups with equal sums is if the largest item equals the sum of the other two (e.g., c = a + b) or if all three are equal (which is a subset of the first case if we consider the 'other two' as the remaining items). Wait, if a=b=c, then a+b = 2a and c=a, so c != a+b. But if a=b=c, total=3a, which is odd unless a=0, but constraints say a>=1. So a=b=c is impossible for equal split. Thus, the only case is one pack equals the sum of the other two. Check if max(a,b,c) == sum(a,b,c) - max(a,b,c).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "8498350670551273305",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507885.8503256
      },
      "rev_n_7_5d0986_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_5d0986_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_5d0986",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the total sum S. If S is odd, output No immediately. Otherwise, check if any single pack equals S/2, or if the sum of any two packs equals S/2. If yes, output Yes; otherwise No.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-4344653831454693415",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507894.4088821
      },
      "rev_n_8_8f8b18_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_8f8b18_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_8f8b18",
        "thought_text": "Since there are only 3 packs, iterate through all 2^3 = 8 possible subsets of packs. Calculate the sum for each subset. If any subset sum equals exactly half the total sum, then a valid distribution exists.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-4344653831454693415",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507894.4088979
      },
      "rev_n_9_e24bcf_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_e24bcf_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_e24bcf",
        "thought_text": "Sort the three values a, b, c. The only possible ways to split 3 items into two non-empty groups with equal sums are: one item vs two items. Check if the largest item equals the sum of the other two, or if the sum of the two smallest equals the largest (which is the same condition).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-4344653831454693415",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507894.408906
      },
